---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
const lastUpdated = '2026-10-29';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy & Optional Service Choices" description="How BanffBound handles optional analytics, advertising and affiliate content, browser storage, newsletter submissions and native referral links. Reopen or change your privacy choices." lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} /></div>
  <section class="section"><div class="container privacy-content">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="privacy-lead">How data and optional services work on BanffBound. Updated <time datetime={lastUpdated}>29 October 2026</time>.</p>
    <p>BanffBound is a travel information and planning website at <strong>banffbound.com</strong>. You can read guides and follow ordinary links without an account. Contact <a href="mailto:hello@banffbound.com">hello@banffbound.com</a> about privacy questions or requests.</p>

    <h2>Your optional service choices</h2>
    <p>Analytics, advertising and affiliate embeds are separate optional categories. They start <strong>off</strong> unless this browser has a valid saved choice enabling them. You can accept all, reject optional services or choose categories individually. Browsing or closing a page does not count as accepting them.</p>
    <button type="button" data-open-consent class="btn btn-primary">Open privacy choices</button>
    <noscript><p>JavaScript is needed to open these controls. Optional tracking scripts and affiliate embeds stay off without it; ordinary guide and provider links remain available.</p></noscript>
    <div class="table-scroll"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">What enabling it allows</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Analytics</th><td>Google Analytics site-usage and interaction measurement, including page and link activity.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Advertising</th><td>Google Ads conversion measurement and Google AdSense advertising services.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Affiliate content</th><td>Optional Expedia and GetYourGuide embedded banners or activity content on relevant pages.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>The same <strong>Privacy choices</strong> control is in the footer. Reopen it to change or withdraw a choice. Turning an enabled category off reloads this page so it starts without that service.</p>
    <p>Withdrawal cannot undo requests already sent or recall information a provider received, including a request already in progress. It does not necessarily remove every cookie a provider previously set. Use the provider’s privacy controls and your browser’s cookie controls as needed.</p>

    <h2>How your choice is saved</h2>
    <p>BanffBound stores the choice in this browser’s <code>localStorage</code> under <code>bb-cookie-consent</code>. The versioned record contains an essential-services flag, the three optional choices and a timestamp. It expires after <strong>365 days</strong>. A missing, expired, malformed or unsupported-version record leaves optional services off and asks for a new choice.</p>
    <p>This is browser storage, not a consent cookie or an account-wide setting. Clearing saved site data removes the durable choice; a temporary tab choice ends when that tab is closed. Another browser or device needs its own choice. If browser storage is blocked, your current choices apply to this page. A temporary all-off marker can be kept with the current tab using the browser’s <code>window.name</code> property. It cannot grant permission. After a reload it keeps optional services off and asks for a new choice, so an older saved grant is not automatically restored after withdrawal. A previous durable choice may still apply in a new tab or future visit if the browser could not replace or remove it; clear the site’s stored data to remove that older choice. If neither saving method is available, the controls explain the limitation and avoid automatically reloading into a known older choice.</p>
    <p>Trip plans, packing checklists and display preferences may use separate first-party browser storage when their tools offer saving. Those functional records are separate from optional tracking choices. Clear them using the tool’s controls where provided or your browser’s site-data settings.</p>

    <h2>Analytics and advertising providers</h2>
    <p>When enabled, Google services may receive information about the browser or device, page visits, interactions and network requests, and may use cookies or similar identifiers. These are not a promise of anonymous processing. BanffBound uses Google Analytics measurement ID <code>G-2DP7J42ZW0</code>, Google Ads <code>AW-17246982814</code> and AdSense publisher ID <code>ca-pub-9022308520000198</code>.</p>
    <p>Provider cookie lifetimes and retention depend on the service and its settings; this page does not promise fixed account-level retention periods. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from partner sites</a>, <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s cookie information</a> and <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google ad controls</a>.</p>

    <h2>Affiliate embeds and ordinary referral links</h2>
    <p>Expedia and GetYourGuide widgets can request content from those providers and use their tracking technologies. Their scripts and widget targets are added only after affiliate content is enabled. Provider content may be unavailable or blocked by the browser; a normal referral link remains available alongside it.</p>
    <p><strong>Following an ordinary affiliate link is a separate action.</strong> The link still opens the provider when optional services are off. It can include BanffBound’s referral or campaign identifier, and the provider can process the visit and use cookies under its own policies and choices. The BanffBound setting does not control the external website or guarantee an untracked visit there.</p>
    <p>BanffBound may earn a commission from qualifying bookings or purchases. Review the relevant provider policy: <a href="https://www.expedia.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Expedia Group</a>, <a href="https://www.getyourguide.com/c/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GetYourGuide</a>, <a href="https://www.vrbo.com/en-ca/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vrbo</a> or <a href="https://www.amazon.ca/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=GX7NJQ4ZB8MHFRNJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Amazon</a>. Check the actual booking terms before paying.</p>

    <h2>Page delivery, images and requested maps</h2>
    <p>Optional choices do not block every third-party request. Delivering a page or remote asset involves sending request information to its server. The site uses services such as Google Fonts and externally hosted images, including Unsplash. A map you choose to load can request its map library and tiles from the named providers. Read the map attribution and provider policies. These delivery and requested-map features are distinct from optional analytics or affiliate embeds.</p>
    <p>Weather and conditions pages display sourced information and links to official reports. They do not require a browser request to OpenWeatherMap or access to your precise device location. When you open an external forecast, camera or report, that service’s policy applies.</p>

    <h2>Newsletter and messages</h2>
    <p>If you submit a newsletter form, the email address and form submission go to Mailchimp using its hosted subscription service. This is an action you choose to take, separate from enabling optional page services. Review <a href="https://www.intuit.com/privacy/statement/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Intuit’s privacy statement, including Mailchimp</a>, and use the unsubscribe option in newsletter messages.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/contact">contact page</a> links to email. Sending a message shares its contents and your email details with the recipient and the email services involved. Do not include sensitive personal information or children’s details in a general travel enquiry. A contact message does not itself subscribe you to the newsletter.</p>

    <h2>Questions and privacy requests</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location and circumstances, you may have rights concerning access, correction, deletion, objections or withdrawal. Email <a href="mailto:hello@banffbound.com">hello@banffbound.com</a> with the request and enough context to identify the information concerned. We may need to verify a request. For information held by an external booking, advertising or subscription service, its own privacy controls and request process also apply.</p>
    <p>If you believe a child has submitted personal information, contact us so the issue can be reviewed. Changes to this policy will be reflected in its review date. If the purpose of optional services changes, we will ask for a new choice.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-content{max-width:820px}.privacy-content h1{margin-bottom:.6rem}.privacy-lead{font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--color-text-light);margin-bottom:1.5rem}.privacy-content h2{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;font-size:1.4rem}.privacy-content p{line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1rem}.privacy-content a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.15em}.privacy-content code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto;margin:1.5rem 0}.comparison-table{min-width:470px}.comparison-table th{text-align:left}.privacy-content .btn{margin:.5rem 0 1rem;color:white;text-decoration:none}
</style>
